#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115056 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/id #uuid "32bd6b27-e95d-5de4-941f-309eb0bc61f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4411" :question/problem "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n![](images/90/90f675ec2a211b6157f040735d551d083c770ac33b5dbfcd74b3678b16d5df53.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-CB & =(A-C)B \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115057 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/id #uuid "3b1395b6-49c1-5e0d-ac94-c2d6fc242f6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4412" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n![](images/de/de98e19bed31050fd07f9979f0428ed4eb90ce05eaff7ba4d19ea81bbd664422.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115058 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "7ab158e6-4222-5cab-88a0-85ce74a7d4b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4413" :question/problem "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\n- $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\n- $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19780864-9003-505a-b598-f3378103858e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263242} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6518a0-5e35-59b6-b899-07522f46b179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 & -21 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263268} {:answer/id #uuid "5517ab5e-f687-5ce4-852d-48dfec575a26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263733} {:answer/id #uuid "55a69114-638a-51d0-954d-1a1fa82cd27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -9 & 24 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263735} {:answer/id #uuid "ce129b66-be90-56f8-b1fe-b394c797c064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce129b66-be90-56f8-b1fe-b394c797c064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264802} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ab1d01-3d95-5a64-a3f9-0807a0efbbe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e430effe-7959-580a-be3d-d4b5f50f0d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-130313" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a610478-68a7-5b53-a8e9-c9393c78345f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a610478-68a7-5b53-a8e9-c9393c78345f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298224} :answer-field/id #uuid "2562ecbb-722e-58dd-b390-5109442e4256" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f164fd8e-50ce-5511-9a10-5d2b4b82a9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f164fd8e-50ce-5511-9a10-5d2b4b82a9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298573} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b7460d1-1a49-56ea-a895-f10a39e37560" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298949} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c50158c8-1a8b-5703-bf99-5124c3377d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c50158c8-1a8b-5703-bf99-5124c3377d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298416} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c988c8-463a-5118-9369-8069b8c8ad56" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4fa12227-09f8-5d99-a2be-207b65a88fe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-319890" :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5380e4f7-3997-5eec-a4c1-2dd08757f0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5380e4f7-3997-5eec-a4c1-2dd08757f0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297904} :answer-field/id #uuid "2488bf7b-4c5f-5b36-8cbb-ca49d28d8bf9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a31a1b-94aa-5cea-9846-cc139c0dc4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a31a1b-94aa-5cea-9846-cc139c0dc4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297589} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ab1180c-fa05-5dcf-b73c-82d0a580b13c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f662dc-9756-5093-86b7-94ddad217ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f662dc-9756-5093-86b7-94ddad217ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297722} :answer-field/id #uuid "a09c47e6-4da3-5f54-947d-4183a7d968e3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5aecc675-116f-5b56-855b-8a2ff5a85c00" :question/math-academy-id "q-319943" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-20-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}78 \\\\ -52 \\\\ -182\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6482cff8-ea84-5d14-a24d-9034a0c7b0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6482cff8-ea84-5d14-a24d-9034a0c7b0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297981} :answer-field/id #uuid "24506a77-9b74-5997-b750-9ae0f37f53de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4004e514-65cc-5ba3-8951-7fdfa32a9481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4004e514-65cc-5ba3-8951-7fdfa32a9481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297805} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fb3cc92-18ef-57d1-8cf8-4873a0f63452" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ac13fb-5f80-5b63-8caf-0023f6f87094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67ac13fb-5f80-5b63-8caf-0023f6f87094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297998} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1529332-216e-5593-b381-6e2408117b50" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34cd5f5a-f82e-5ae5-899e-5e1bd32cf8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-320021" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $(AB)$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)\\,C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 48 & -60\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0768e386-ed42-523a-8b81-d32778b33888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 18 & 9 \\\\ 21 & 7 & -42 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324039} {:answer/id #uuid "5765f40b-6dcf-5301-9949-f4819aec1ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 42 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324697} {:answer/id #uuid "8bca11ec-165a-537d-b134-38df44b671e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 9 & -42 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325158} {:answer/id #uuid "a36dc3f4-9f65-59e6-9311-6f889cfc4cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325358} {:answer/id #uuid "f31eb4fa-cff2-5b17-9422-8db3c6117a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a36dc3f4-9f65-59e6-9311-6f889cfc4cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325358} :answer-field/id #uuid "b79923e4-1da4-5e24-8a5e-c420b9db32e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0594dca0-de16-5429-abef-c4b9b45aec7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42001" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ae122ef-fb08-5ffb-b2a0-2df28bb4b383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113954} {:answer/id #uuid "3397c57d-ebd7-50f9-8ce9-6ee8d2308688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\