which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n- **II.** $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n- **III.** $AC+BC=(A+B)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b4b6c9-b120-5669-8778-9d44bd03a705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451627} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9ff174-54f1-5fc0-82c9-56c7f68be83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9ff174-54f1-5fc0-82c9-56c7f68be83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451628} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6596886-eb35-5a15-8678-0d03898ac57c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b1b7dcd-0a45-5a31-b1e7-359ba6b8ce48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451629} {:answer/id #uuid "2844641e-66b1-56cc-8371-e36f6a1b3ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b7dcd-0a45-5a31-b1e7-359ba6b8ce48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451629} :answer-field/id #uuid "648f05bf-a002-5add-8c9a-e67860f117ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aec13ecc-22bc-5436-b215-dddd0d181f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451631} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfc103f-6039-5ed8-b224-6f15716dcaa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aec13ecc-22bc-5436-b215-dddd0d181f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451631} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce1dbe9-397b-565f-a4c9-e832cb32d032" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c88851c-8567-55d2-897e-8b0f9b020c35" :question/math-academy-id "q-75662" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A(B+C)=AC+AB$\n- **II.** $A(BC)=(BA)C$\n- **III.** $AB=BA$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\nA(B+C)=AB+AC=AC+AB\n$$\n\n since matrix addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC)=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d29adab0-49f5-5be8-9dfb-41b652b9f78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451639} {:answer/id #uuid "aae53705-b1e7-5ad4-a458-fc12bd5715e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d29adab0-49f5-5be8-9dfb-41b652b9f78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ec2f6a3-b7c4-5dbf-b313-e1460364d497" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "163312b5-47ae-51a4-8302-780627f27eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451641} {:answer/id #uuid "8391eb9d-de48-5257-958c-71e626ee3926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "163312b5-47ae-51a4-8302-780627f27eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451641} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e9e4ab6-972e-5a28-8a06-204e593f15c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5abcda23-f4db-5653-8749-2127e4eb2cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451643} {:answer/id #uuid "83789ace-8be4-5fa7-bb78-667b324a5f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83789ace-8be4-5fa7-bb78-667b324a5f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451644} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebdef35b-4dc7-5168-954f-85f588629353" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ca7b9cd-e052-55a9-b9b9-9f438a40909d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75717" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $CB=BC$\n- **II.** $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- **III.** $A(BC)=(AB)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statement  III is true."}]}
